BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Current Events Discussion Group
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261113T123000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6a5a9bfec44ff5b82cf5e5fa@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us every second Friday of the month for a Current Events 
 Discussion group from August to November. Each month\, we will select an 
 article to read from publications like The Atlantic\, The New Yorker\, The
  Guardian\, The New York Times\, The Wall Street Journal\, and New York Ma
 gazine. You can access all these resources digitally with your library car
 d. \n\nRegistration is required\, and participants will be emailed the ar
 ticles on the Monday before each meeting. If you need help accessing these
  resources\, please reach out to atherton@smcl.org.\n\nAges: Adult program
  (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: requir
 ed\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9bfec44ff5b82cf5e5fa
 \nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a5a9bfec44ff5b82cf5e5fa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Winter Music Festival: Rob Hart Trio
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261217T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261217T190000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6ad7d69a9dbc2b002c8fed8d@local-events
DESCRIPTION:The Rob Hart Trio delivers a genre-blending jazz experience th
 at’s as adventurous as it is intimate. Rooted in organic traditional jaz
 z and energized by fusion\, funk\, Latin grooves\, and textural experiment
 ation\, the trio creates high-powered\, on-the-edge improvisations that ke
 ep audiences engaged from the first note to the last. Since the early 1990
 s\, the group has evolved through multiple instrumental lineups\, constant
 ly exploring new musical pathways. Between songs\, Rob brings listeners in
 side the music with behind-the-scenes stories and inspiration\, turning ev
 ery performance into a personal\, immersive journey."\n\nAges: Adult progr
 am (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none
 \nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d69a9dbc2b002c8fed8d\n
 Last synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d69a9dbc2b002c8fed8d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Winter Music Festival: David Rocha Jazz
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T190000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6ad7d6029d27a000455239c8@local-events
DESCRIPTION:David Rocha Jazz plays an eclectic mix of modern jazz composit
 ions\, drawing from over three hundred tunes in our library.  This include
 s bossa nova\, swing\, jazz rock\, Latin\, jazz waltz\, ballads\, and blu
 es.  In addition to arranging the melodies\, we all take individual solos 
 on the specific chord changes each melody is based on. David Rocha Jazz s
 olos aren’t written out or memorized.  They are all improvised spontaneo
 usly\, which makes jazz such a unique art form.\n\nAges: Adult program (ki
 ds welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSour
 ce: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d6029d27a000455239c8\nLast s
 ynced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d6029d27a000455239c8
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] 1:1 Genealogy Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261105T163000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-69374f086724c63d00e5ee31@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Are\n you ready to uncover the fascinating stories of your anc
 estors? Join us\n for personalized 30-minute genealogy sessions that will 
 ignite your \npassion for family history!  \n\n\n\nWhat Awaits You:  \nAnc
 estry Library Edition: Unlock billions of records and start weaving your f
 amily tree! HeritageHub: Dive into captivating tales about your ancestors 
 and your local history. HeritageQuest: Discover hidden gems like census re
 cords\, military documents\, and so much more!My China Roots: Explore your
  family history with My China Roots\, a Chinese genealogy website and data
 base.\nYour Journey Starts Here! Your\n suggested appointment date & time 
 are all TENTATIVE until you \nreceive an email confirmation. Whether you'r
 e a beginner or a seasoned \nresearcher\, our sessions are designed to hel
 p you uncover your unique \nstory. Reserve your spot now and embark on the
  adventure of discovering \nyour roots! \n\n \nREGISTER HERE\n\nAges: Adul
 t program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistratio
 n: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/69374f086724c63d00e
 5ee31\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/69374f086724c63d00e5ee31
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Open Sewing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261123T143000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6a97468d341bb11431ee6a2c@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for open time to use the library’s sewing machines. 
 Bring your own project or pick from previous library sewing projects. Need
 les\, thread\, iron\, and cutting tools are provided for use in the librar
 y. No fabric is provided except for scraps. This program is intended for i
 ndividuals who can use the sewing machines independently. There will be n
 o formal instruction.\n\n\nThis program is open only to adults 18+.\n\nNo 
 registration required\, as time and space permit.\n\nAges: Adult program (
 kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSo
 urce: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a97468d341bb11431ee6a2c\nLast
