BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Seasonal Tai Chi: Winter Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270120T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270120T113000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b0@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Chen-style Taijiquan (Tai Chi) is widely acknowledged as the a
 ncestor of all other styles of Taijiquan. This class will introduce the Ch
 en-style Taijiquan form\, Silk-reeling Exercises and Wuji Qigong. The Chen
 -style Taijiquan form is soft and graceful with strong rooted stands that 
 will help students to develop strength\, balance\, coordination and an und
 erstanding of basic Taiji principles. Silk-reeling Exercises are a series 
 of spiral movements that promote muscle relaxation and flexibility by redu
 cing physical tension and strain. Wuji Qigong (standing meditation) will h
 elp students to cultivate internal energy (qi) with proper body alignment 
 for better internal energy flow\, which will enhance their immune systems 
 and reduce physical and mental stress.\n\nPlease use the following form to
  signup for email updates and an last-minute schedule changes. Registratio
 n is encouraged\, but it is not required.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids wel
 come to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: ht
 tps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b0\nLast synced:
  2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Cookbook Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270408T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270408T190000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6a6d051d88e9bf280034ac86@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Do you love food and cooking? Join us for the Cookbook Book Cl
 ub\,\n where each month we explore a new cookbook\, try out recipes\, and 
 share \nour experiences. The featured cookbook will be available for check
 out at the\n meeting. \n\n*NOTE: for this month\, the Cookbook Club will t
 ake place on the first Thursday of the month.\n\n\nVisit our Cookbook Book
  Club Info Hub      to find out more! \n\nNo registration is required at t
 his time. This book club is for adults ages 18+.\n\nAges: Adult program (k
 ids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSou
 rce: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a6d051d88e9bf280034ac86\nLast 
 synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a6d051d88e9bf280034ac86
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] de Young Museum Art Talk: Treasures of the Pharaohs
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261119T173000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6ae09458fee2d21deb260001@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the Friends of Atherton Library as we welcome a docent fr
 om the de Young Museum for a talk about the museum's exhibit on Treasures 
 of the Pharaohs. The exhibit features exquisite works that exemplify the
  grandeur of the world of the Egyptian pharaohs. The objects range from m
 onumental granite statues to intricate gold jewelry\, each highlighting t
 he wealth and complexity of ancient Egyptian civilization. Spanning 3000 y
 ears of history\, the exhibition begins with the pharaoh at the apex of E
 gypt’s social hierarchy and broadens to include his family\, high offi
 cials\, beliefs\, gods\, and views of death and the afterlife. \n\n\n\nThe
  exhibit will be open through January 11\, 2027 at the de Young Museum in 
 San Francisco. Registration is encouraged but not required.\n\nAges: Adult
  program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration
 : required\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ae09458fee2d21d
 eb260001\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ae09458fee2d21deb260001
END:VEVENT
