BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Fall in Love With the Classics at Holbrook Palmer Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T113000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6a04dac9025b99d84474f8e2@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join this fall for a three-part book discussion series explori
 ng love\, ambition\, and social expectations through classic literature. T
 his limited-run series invites readers to examine how relationships and cl
 ass shape personal choices.\n\nWe’ll meet monthly from August through No
 vember on the third Wednesday of the month for welcoming and engaging conv
 ersations. Books will be provided. Attendance at each discussion meeting 
 is required in order to receive the next book in the series. \n\nJoin us f
 or the concluding discussion in our classic literature series. During this
  final meeting\, we will discuss Edith Wharton’s The House of Mirth\, ex
 ploring its themes of ambition\, social pressure\, class\, and personal fr
 eedom as Lily Bart navigates the glittering yet fragile world of New York 
 society. This will be the final discussion meeting of the series.\n\nThe b
 ook club will meet at: North Meadow Picnic Tables at Holbrook Palmer Park.
 \n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them
 )\nRegistration: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a04d
 ac9025b99d84474f8e2\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a04dac9025b99d84474f8e2
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Seasonal Tai Chi: Winter Session
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270127T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270127T113000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b1@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Chen-style Taijiquan (Tai Chi) is widely acknowledged as the a
 ncestor of all other styles of Taijiquan. This class will introduce the Ch
 en-style Taijiquan form\, Silk-reeling Exercises and Wuji Qigong. The Chen
 -style Taijiquan form is soft and graceful with strong rooted stands that 
 will help students to develop strength\, balance\, coordination and an und
 erstanding of basic Taiji principles. Silk-reeling Exercises are a series 
 of spiral movements that promote muscle relaxation and flexibility by redu
 cing physical tension and strain. Wuji Qigong (standing meditation) will h
 elp students to cultivate internal energy (qi) with proper body alignment 
 for better internal energy flow\, which will enhance their immune systems 
 and reduce physical and mental stress.\n\nPlease use the following form to
  signup for email updates and an last-minute schedule changes. Registratio
 n is encouraged\, but it is not required.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids wel
 come to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: none\nSource: ht
 tps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b1\nLast synced:
  2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aa31b1e8cf597003f92f2b1
END:VEVENT
