SUMMARY:[ATH] Holiday Floral Arrangement Demonstration
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261118T150000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6ada4fa5de300e00451c200c@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join San Mateo County Libraries and the Atherton Garden Guild
  for beautiful holiday floral arrangements. The class will be taught by fl
 oral arrangers Nancy Butler and Kathy Ladra. \n\nNancy\, a past President
  and Program Chair of the Atherton Garden Guild\, and she is an avid gar
 dener and floral arranger who enjoys travel. She currently arranges flower
 s for Gamble Gardens. \n\nKathy Ladra has been a floral arranger for over
  35 years. She studied under Virginia Farewell and Ann Patrick. She had be
 en part of the Filoli Floral Design Program\, president of the Atherton Ga
 rden Guild\,  and President of Gamble Garden.\n\nRegistration will open o
 n Wednesday\, October 28 at 6:00 PM.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome 
 to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: htt
 ps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ada4fa5de300e00451c200c\nLast synced: 
 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ada4fa5de300e00451c200c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Winter Music Festival: Dan Ashley - News Anchor and Rock Sta
 r!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261209T130000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6ad7d66a9dbc2b002c8fed66@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Dan Ashley\, the longtime ABC7 evening news anchor/reporter\, 
 is also a Rock Star! Dan looks forward to returning to several San Mateo C
 ounty Libraries since last year and is excited to add performances at new 
 ones. He has spent many hours in both public and university libraries and 
 is honored to bring his storytelling\, through his original\, remarkable s
 ongs\, to everyone at the county libraries. Dan is a recording artist and 
 will sing accompanied by his amazing guitarist\, Jeff Tamelier\, who was t
 he longtime touring guitarist for Tower of Power and Starship. Together\, 
 they will bring an unforgettable acoustic performance of contemporary Coun
 try/Americana Rock music\, including originals heard online and on the rad
 io\, as well as familiar covers. Come join us\, sing along\, clap your han
 ds\, stomp your feet\, bob your heads\, and get ready to Rock!\n\nAges: Ad
 ult program (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistrat
 ion: none\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d66a9dbc2b002
 c8fed66\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ad7d66a9dbc2b002c8fed66
END:VEVENT
