SUMMARY:[ATH] Bamboo\, Blooms & Blessings: A Year of the Goat Calligraphy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270124T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20270124T163000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6abadb1c29c3d600332c40f8@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate the arrival of the Year of the Goat through Chinese 
 culture\, calligraphy\, and hands-on creativity! Participants will learn a
 bout traditional Lunar New Year customs\, including the tradition of decor
 ating the home with flowers to welcome the new year. \n\nStep-by-step\, pa
 rticipants will create a unique hanging decoration by arranging faux flowe
 rs into traditional Chinese bamboo strips\, inspired by bamboo weaving\, a
 n important part of Chinese craft heritage. They will also learn to write 
 auspicious New Year phrases and draw adorable little goats to personalize 
 their artwork. Each participant will take home a one-of-a-kind handmade de
 coration\, perfect for hanging at home to welcome the Year of the Goat wit
 h flowers\, blessings\, and creativity!\n\nDue to high demand\, we ask tha
 t community members signup for a single occurrence of this series to so th
 at as many community members can participate in this experience as possibl
 e. Registration is required to attend\, and registration opens on Sunday
 \, January 3 at 6:00pm.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome to tag along
 \, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: https://smcl.bi
 bliocommons.com/events/6abadb1c29c3d600332c40f8\nLast synced: 2026-10-28 1
 1:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6abadb1c29c3d600332c40f8
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Painting Diwali Diyas
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261108T130000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Diyas [De-ah] are a form of clay lanterns used across India\, 
 not only to light our religious altars but to light our homes and public s
 paces during Diwali- the Festival of Lights. These lights indicate that go
 od prevails over evil and that a period of peace is coming. Workshop part
 icipants will receive a brief history lesson on what Diwali is\, the story
  behind it\, and how it is celebrated across the Indian diaspora (in India
  and around the world). Afterward\, participants will be guided on differe
 nt ways to paint their Diyas and shown how to light them at home.\n\nDue t
 o high demand\, we ask that community members sign up for a single occurre
 nce of this series so that as many community members can participate in th
 is experience as possible. Registration is required to attend\, and it ope
 ns on Sunday\, October 25 at 10:00am.\n\nAges: Adult program (kids welcome
  to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: required\nSource: ht
 tps://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826\nLast synced:
  2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6a88bb6a4cb69d003e226826
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[ATH] Health Portals: Managing Your Healthcare Online
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261104T130000
DTSTAMP:20261028T184231Z
UID:smcl-6aaeeaaf6074830038282498@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an engaging session designed for adults and senior
 s who want to feel more confident using their healthcare provider’s onli
 ne portal. Learn how to use health portals to communicate with your doctor
 ’s office\, manage appointments\, and access important health informatio
 n from your smartphone\, tablet\, or computer. Perfect for those comfortab
 le with basic device navigation.\n\nTopics include:\n Logging in safely (
 passwords\, verification codes\, and avoiding scams)Sending messages to yo
 ur doctor’s office and knowing what to message vs. call aboutScheduling
 \, rescheduling\, and canceling appointmentsJoining video visits and prepa
 ring for virtual appointmentsViewing test results\, visit summaries\, and 
 after-visit instructionsRequesting medication refills and checking medicat
 ion listsUploading photos/documents (insurance cards\, symptoms\, forms) t
 hrough the portalPresented by Amy Culpepper of PepTech.\n\nAges: Adult pro
 gram (kids welcome to tag along\, not designed for them)\nRegistration: no
 ne\nSource: https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aaeeaaf6074830038282498
 \nLast synced: 2026-10-28 11:42 PDT
LOCATION:Atherton Library\, 2 Dinkelspiel Station Ln\, Atherton\, CA 94027
URL:https://smcl.bibliocommons.com/events/6aaeeaaf6074830038282498
END:VEVENT
